From 388338689fedd878b1a7b2a899f4b9797b53fc23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Hill-Tanners <j.d.tanner@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Mar 2026 21:46:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] elan: add driver for ELAN 04f3:0c7f fingerprint sensor
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds a new image-based driver for the ELAN Microelectronics 0c7f USB
fingerprint sensor, following the swipe-style capture model used by
other ELAN drivers in libfprint.

The driver handles USB bulk transfers for frame capture, assembles
partial frames into a composite portrait image (52x150 px), and
submits it to libfprint's NBIS minutiae pipeline for enrollment and
verification.

Notable design choices:
* FP_DEVICE_FEATURE_IDENTIFY is explicitly disabled — the device
  firmware does not support 1:N identification, only 1:1 verification.
  Leaving it enabled caused fprintd to crash during first enrollment.
* A deactivating flag defers frame_buf/best_img cleanup until after all
  in-flight USB transfers have completed, avoiding a use-after-free when
  dev_deactivate is called while the capture SSM is still running.
* Image quality is scored per-frame and the best frame is selected;
  frames are Gaussian-blurred and 16-bit pixel values are scaled to
  8-bit using the per-frame min/max range.

Tested on Fedora 43, Wayland, with fprintd 1.94.5:
  fprintd-enroll, GNOME Settings fingerprint enrollment, PAM auth.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libfprint/drivers/elan0c7f.c | 814 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libfprint/meson.build        |   2 +
 meson.build                  |   2 +
 3 files changed, 818 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libfprint/drivers/elan0c7f.c

